  "body": "These three steps were previously only performed for history.pushState()/history.replaceState(), but they need to be performed for all callers of the URL and history update steps, the other one being document.open().\n\nFor the serializedData steps, this is editorial, as document.open() does not pass serializedData. But for updating the latest entry, it's a bug fix, as otherwise things get strangely out of sync.\n\nReview from @natechapin would be appreciated, as well as editor review.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/6459/history.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 5, 2021, 10:33 PM UTC (69caa80)\">/history.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/6459/1398653...69caa80/history.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 5, 2021, 10:33 PM UTC (69caa80)\">diff</a> )",
